From 71a5ddd5c1b01de12386e4fe59f7eef965761e43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:11:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] feat(registry): write resource change events in the
 write transaction

Every resource write of SQLiteRegistry (create, update, status write,
delete request, delete) now also writes a DomainEvent into the outbox
that shares the registry's connection, inside the same transaction as
the resource row and its change record: a failed write leaves no event,
and a failed event write rolls the resource write back.

The envelope follows api/schemas/event.schema.json. eventType is
"<kind as dotted words>.<change>" (inference.service.created, .updated,
.status_updated, .terminating, .deleted); data carries the kind, the
resource identity, the phase and the resource representation after the
write (deleted: the last state before the delete). Writes without a
correlation id get a generated one.

The controller passes the correlation id of a reconcile to its status
writes, and the reconciler passes it (and actor "reconciler") when it
removes the release finalizer, so all events of one reconcile share it.

delete() now reads the row under BEGIN IMMEDIATE before deleting it to
capture the last state. CONTROL_PLANE_VERSION moves to a dependency-free
version module (still re-exported by app) so the registry can use it as
producer.version without an import cycle.
